---
import Agents from "../components/Agents.astro";
import Burrow from "../components/Burrow.astro";
import Collections from "../components/Collections.astro";
import Compare from "../components/Compare.astro";
import Demo from "../components/Demo.astro";
import Download from "../components/Download.astro";
import Faq from "../components/Faq.astro";
import Features from "../components/Features.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import Hero from "../components/Hero.astro";
import Nav from "../components/Nav.astro";
import Outro from "../components/Outro.astro";
import Pricing from "../components/Pricing.astro";
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { belowHeader, shots } from "../shots";
---

<Base>
  <Nav />
  <main>
    <Hero />

    <Compare
      id="features"
      shot={shots.highlight}
      crop={{ x: 255, y: 150, w: 840, h: 525 }}
      narrow={{ crop: { x: 266, y: 342, w: 500, h: 312 } }}
      alt="QRabbit with a passage selected in the paper and the Explore toolbar above it, and an earlier thread's highlight further up the page."
    >
      <Fragment slot="title">No more copying text. <em>Just highlight it.</em></Fragment>
      <Fragment slot="lede">
        Select a passage and choose Explore. The thread opens beside the paper with the passage and the text around it
        already in hand, and the highlight stays in the paper as your way back to it.
      </Fragment>
      <div class="u">So how do the four value functions relate?</div>
      <div class="a">
        The optimal ones are the best the on-policy ones can be, <i>V</i>*(<i>s</i>) = max<sub>π</sub>
        <i>V</i><sup>π</sup>(<i>s</i>), and the same holds for <i>Q</i>. Each can be written in terms of the other…
      </div>
      <div class="keys"><kbd>Ctrl</kbd><kbd>C</kbd> in the paper → <kbd>Alt</kbd><kbd>Tab</kbd> → <kbd>Ctrl</kbd><kbd>V</kbd></div>
      <div class="u paste">
        <q>In deep RL, we deal with parameterized policies: policies whose outputs are computable functions that depend on a set of parameters</q>
        What does this mean?
      </div>
      <div class="a">Which text is this from? Without the paragraphs around it, I can only guess what the parameters are.</div>
      <div class="u lost">It's from the Spinning Up page I pasted earlier. Section 3, I think?</div>
    </Compare>

    <Compare
      id="lists"
      shot={shots.thread}
      crop={belowHeader(shots.thread)}
      narrow={{ shot: shots.threadNarrow, crop: belowHeader(shots.threadNarrow) }}
      up="The first list is three answers up"
      alt="A QRabbit thread answering 'What are the main ways to learn a good policy?' with a numbered list. Two of its points are highlighted as branches, and the outline above the thread lists them under it."
    >
      <Fragment slot="title">AI loves a list. <em>Keep them tidy.</em></Fragment>
      <Fragment slot="lede">
        When an answer has several parts, AI reaches for a list, and following up on each point turns one chat into a
        tangle of lists inside lists. In QRabbit you highlight a point and it opens its own branch. The outline keeps every
        branch in order, and the answer stays where it was.
      </Fragment>
      <div class="a">
        <ol start="3">
          <li><b>Actor-critic methods</b> combine the two…</li>
          <li><b>Model-based methods</b> plan with a learned model…</li>
        </ol>
      </div>
      <div class="u">Go deeper on 3.</div>
      <div class="a">
        It comes down to three ideas:
        <ol>
          <li><b>The actor</b> picks actions from the policy…</li>
          <li><b>The critic</b> scores them against a baseline…</li>
          <li><b>The advantage</b> says how much better than usual…</li>
        </ol>
      </div>
      <div class="u">Why does 2 cut the variance?</div>
      <div class="a">Do you mean the critic here, or value-based methods, point 2 in the first list?</div>
      <div class="u lost">The critic. And what was 4 in the first list again?</div>
    </Compare>

    <Burrow />
    <Demo />
    <Features />
    <Collections />
    <Agents />
    <Pricing />
    <Download />
    <Faq />
    <Outro />
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Base>
